<p>Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Cardinal Pierbattista Pizzaballa, the Latin Patriarch of Jerusalem, would receive &quot;full and immediate access&quot; to the Church of the Holy Sepulchre after Israeli police blocked him and Friar Francesco Ielpo on Palm Sunday. Church officials said it was the first time in centuries that church leaders had been unable to celebrate Palm Sunday Mass there. The confrontation came under wartime emergency conditions in Jerusalem, where repeated missile fire during the war with Iran had put the city on alert. Netanyahu’s order restored access a day after the block.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/j0MNMuFhnoB0dkNQ_xMwXWdVgjQrbjWVyzPfxml0dlV1FgcurP8wlDJgw9YzZITVvqcS8zG8kEKIzSGKBrem68OCvn9vW7j4pwlMaX0HPJsDBWnyxqdl4z7j38JW-Bcqrqf-8lBBjx-iXYkBk_SWC4LczKYvbW_YYg9cWBdF8YsQ2D4Uds3sB5iruJOxSI8B_yTcOQCt950dkKyq6R9-Ikg-10U' alt='Cardinal Pierbattista Pizzaballa leads a Palm Sunday prayer service in Jerusalem amid restrictions on large gatherings.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Private service: Several reports said the blocked Palm Sunday ceremony was meant to be a private Mass, not a large public gathering, sharpening the dispute over whether the restrictions were necessary.</li><li>Old City risk: BBC reported that officials asked Pizzaballa not to enter the church out of concern for his safety in the Old City during heightened wartime risk.</li><li>Rapid backlash: Le Monde reported that the Palm Sunday block drew worldwide uproar, helping explain why Netanyahu intervened publicly the next day instead of leaving the dispute to local authorities.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli police: Police said they had notified church authorities in advance that no Palm Sunday Mass could be held because major holy sites were closed and large gatherings were banned for safety reasons during the Iran war. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-police-block-catholic-leaders-from-palm-sunday-mass-in-jerusalem/a-76586194'>DW</a>, <a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/israeli-police-prevent-catholic-leaders-from-celebrating-palm-sunday-mass-at-church-in-jerusalem'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Latin Patriarchate of Jerusalem: The Patriarchate said police stopped Pizzaballa and Ielpo as they walked to the church and called the decision manifestly unreasonable and grossly disproportionate. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israeli-police-block-catholic-cardinal-from-jerusalems-holy-sepulchre-on-palm-sunday/article70800428.ece'>The Hindu</a>, <a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3348322/israeli-police-prevent-catholic-leaders-celebrating-palm-sunday-mass-jerusalem'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Benjamin Netanyahu: In a public post on X, Netanyahu said he had instructed the relevant authorities to give the Latin Patriarch full and immediate access to the church. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/latin-patriarch-get-immediate-access-holy-sepulchre-netanyahu'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/israeli-police-prevent-catholic-leaders-from-celebrating-palm-sunday-mass-at-church-in-jerusalem'>Israeli police prevent Catholic leaders from celebrating Palm Sunday Mass at church in Jerusalem</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/church-holy-sepulchre-jerusalem-cardinal-pizzaballa-israel-catholic/'>Cardinal temporarily barred from entering Jerusalem&#x27;s Church of Holy Sepulchre</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israeli-police-block-catholic-cardinal-from-jerusalems-holy-sepulchre-on-palm-sunday/article70800428.ece'>Israeli police block Catholic cardinal from Jerusalem&#x27;s Holy Sepulchre on Palm Sunday</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/29/world/middleeast/catholic-church-jerusalem.html'>Catholic Leaders Barred From Jerusalem Holy Site on Palm Sunday</a> - nyti